{"title":"2021 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 13","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1_(Three_Right_Triangles)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1 (Three Right Triangles)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(One_Right_Triangle)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (One Right Triangle)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Trirectangular_Tetrahedron)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Trirectangular Tetrahedron)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Remark\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Remark</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_(Simple_&amp;_Quick)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution (Simple &amp; Quick)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Omega_Learn_(Using_Pythagorean_Theorem,_3D_Geometry:_Tetrahedron)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Omega Learn (Using Pythagorean Theorem, 3D Geometry: Tetrahedron)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_TheBeautyofMath\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by TheBeautyofMath</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>What is the volume of tetrahedron <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> with edge lengths <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/7/7676bb86e9162142043f19c0502c5bf05e69f5dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB = 2$\" width=\"61\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/0/9b02c59949a90402d95f555f5802f39e8c55ffcf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC = 3$\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/d/62d592f9a0bd33b27454c6612300587ffe447083.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"62\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/d/aed738037e081c4c3e8caeb61af86cd6890d3ea8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC = \\sqrt{13}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"88\" height=\"21\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/8/4381ebf1d481768a9df3049b088c8d5e3150d12c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BD = 2\\sqrt{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"88\" height=\"18\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/9/4d99eb629f027ee953f4fce4c24425c6fb800a24.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD = 5$\" width=\"62\" height=\"12\" />&#160;?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/b/6db849989b30ef58962c2b2015cf79696a6e7aee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)} ~3 \\qquad\\textbf{(B)} ~2\\sqrt{3} \\qquad\\textbf{(C)} ~4\\qquad\\textbf{(D)} ~3\\sqrt{3}\\qquad\\textbf{(E)} ~6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"397\" height=\"21\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_1_.28Three_Right_Triangles.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1_(Three_Right_Triangles)\">Solution 1 (Three Right Triangles)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1 (Three Right Triangles)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Drawing the tetrahedron out and testing side lengths, we realize that the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/9/0c94274851bd83704cd5d3ee28548bfaa906262e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ACD, \\triangle ABC,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"132\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/5/f75d6d58b03031bd7cb52a7ca886a8ddf369d21c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" /> are right triangles by the Converse of the Pythagorean Theorem. It is now easy to calculate the volume of the tetrahedron using the formula for the volume of a pyramid. If we take <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/e/b8eabc87afe4c11a47e4aa27628d5517af4866b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ADC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> as the base, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/0/840e2b592390eb6ec918fa6f3292716ce170de66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AB}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> must be the altitude. The volume of tetrahedron <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/9/189668fd62e0d285f2257ca0ad69c4575b8908ef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{1}{3} \\cdot \\dfrac{3 \\cdot 4}{2} \\cdot 2=\\boxed{\\textbf{(C)} ~4}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"169\" height=\"38\" />\nThis solution does not have a reasoning for using triangle ADC as base\n~Icewolf10 ~Bakedpotato66 ~MRENTHUSIASM\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28One_Right_Triangle.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(One_Right_Triangle)\">Solution 2 (One Right Triangle)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (One Right Triangle)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We will place tetrahedron <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> in the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/7/d57d8fef9329fabd73078ae824a034e8a00e332f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$xyz$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"28\" height=\"11\" />-plane. By the Converse of the Pythagorean Theorem, we know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/7/0f7a55113a84ee4c04eb66f66d08310c32533ca2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ACD$\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" /> is a right triangle. Without the loss of generality, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/d/9bdc7c700d903d7cc4e93de9ad4bc6167b86a993.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A=(0,0,0), C=(3,0,0), D=(0,4,0),$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"309\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/d/61dbcede3c5a473a47f4371cf63e26334ee91f53.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B=(x,y,z).$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"102\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>We apply the Distance Formula to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/e/41e9f0f54dc38ebafa3e7250708b28a86d6f1a3d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BA},\\overline{BC},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"69\" height=\"19\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/e/2ae4f866671229c5e8a6b7c2bc5ef859c3214820.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BD},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"34\" height=\"19\" /> respectively:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/d/f5d8f1258aed544c048c97c73b0cb8dedd2cd72f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} x^2+y^2+z^2&amp;=2^2, &amp;(1) \\\\ (x-3)^2+y^2+z^2&amp;=\\sqrt{13}^2, &amp;(2) \\\\ x^2+(y-4)^2+z^2&amp;=\\left(2\\sqrt5\\right)^2. &amp;\\hspace{1mm} (3) \\end{align*}\" width=\"333\" height=\"96\" />\nSubtracting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/9/0d9c3b1c142cbd3f8217dabc160c57e4750df241.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"18\" /> from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/f/62f62a19f0425d8e6121ca0c1cfd3ce96e43c9c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"18\" /> gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/d/10d1dbbd4d93ae6e403705d73c0509e8ffa5d9c7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-6x+9=9,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"105\" height=\"17\" /> from which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/b/afbd257ea8fb161c48d8b97ba051decdb268fb34.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=0.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>Subtracting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/9/0d9c3b1c142cbd3f8217dabc160c57e4750df241.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"18\" /> from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/8/b88ea3916e8089c7edbccc3ff91e58e01a6e2682.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"18\" /> gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/3/2e39f5402e43ccda45354013c16a128f708b55af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-8y+16=16,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"119\" height=\"16\" /> from which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/9/21989b1ff1334711407360d7b56cc21f1bbe02e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=0.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"46\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p>Substituting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/0/9d0338cdad4134e835145541ef1f0bc401796a94.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x,y)=(0,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"105\" height=\"18\" /> into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/9/0d9c3b1c142cbd3f8217dabc160c57e4750df241.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"18\" /> produces <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/7/6672171d87ec5a7a17a8549c7e22f88f238145e0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z^2=4,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"54\" height=\"18\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/c/53c46846b95c9e5d621e52d3786427e4f5280e2f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|z|=2.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"56\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Let the brackets denote areas. Finally, we find the volume of tetrahedron <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> using <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/7/0f7a55113a84ee4c04eb66f66d08310c32533ca2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ACD$\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" /> as the base:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/4/8f4027a0d67a9da4b7acccad4ed81fdca7fadd30.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} V_{ABCD}&amp;=\\frac13\\cdot[ACD]\\cdot h_B \\\\ &amp;=\\frac13\\cdot\\left(\\frac12\\cdot AC \\cdot AD\\right)\\cdot |z| \\\\ &amp;=\\boxed{\\textbf{(C)} ~4}. \\end{align*}\" width=\"256\" height=\"121\" />\n~MRENTHUSIASM\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Trirectangular_Tetrahedron.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Trirectangular_Tetrahedron)\">Solution 3 (Trirectangular Tetrahedron)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Trirectangular Tetrahedron)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://mathworld.wolfram.com/TrirectangularTetrahedron.html\">https://mathworld.wolfram.com/TrirectangularTetrahedron.html</a>\n</p><p>Given the observations from Solution 1, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/9/0c94274851bd83704cd5d3ee28548bfaa906262e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ACD, \\triangle ABC,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"132\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/5/f75d6d58b03031bd7cb52a7ca886a8ddf369d21c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" /> are right triangles, the base is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/5/94585e5639fd985bbe71e9039a8681af8e09d680.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABD.$\" width=\"63\" height=\"13\" /> We can apply the information about a trirectangular tetrahedron (all of the face angles are right angles), which states that the volume is\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/1/7a13dd4acea701f058c3d7b1abcb18e39f485b0e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} V&amp;=\\frac16\\cdot AB\\cdot AC\\cdot BD \\\\ &amp;=\\frac16\\cdot2\\cdot4\\cdot3 \\\\ &amp;=\\boxed{\\textbf{(C)} ~4}. \\end{align*}\" width=\"176\" height=\"114\" />\n~AMC60 (Solution)\n</p><p>~MRENTHUSIASM (Revision)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Remark\">Remark</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Remark\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Here is a similar problem from another AMC test: <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2015 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 21\">2015 AMC 10A Problem 21</a>.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_.28Simple_.26_Quick.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_(Simple_&amp;_Quick)\">Video Solution (Simple &amp; Quick)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution (Simple &amp; Quick)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/bRrchiDCrKE\">https://youtu.be/bRrchiDCrKE</a>\n</p><p>~ Education, the Study of Everything\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_by_Omega_Learn_.28Using_Pythagorean_Theorem.2C_3D_Geometry:_Tetrahedron.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Omega_Learn_(Using_Pythagorean_Theorem,_3D_Geometry:_Tetrahedron)\">Video Solution by Omega Learn (Using Pythagorean Theorem, 3D Geometry: Tetrahedron)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Omega Learn (Using Pythagorean Theorem, 3D Geometry: Tetrahedron)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/i4yUaXVUWKE\">https://youtu.be/i4yUaXVUWKE</a>\n</p><p>~ pi_is_3.14\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_TheBeautyofMath\">Video Solution by TheBeautyofMath</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by TheBeautyofMath\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/t-EEP2V4nAE?t=813\">https://youtu.be/t-EEP2V4nAE?t=813</a>\n</p><p>~IceMatrix\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_10A\" title=\"2021 AMC 10A\">2021 AMC 10A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_10A_Problems\" title=\"2021 AMC 10A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_10A_Answer_Key\" title=\"2021 AMC 10A Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_12\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2021 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 12\">Problem 12</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_14\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2021 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 14\">Problem 14</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/w